{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778561838643,"sessionID":"ses_1e5750b97ffe2Ms6mBm22tkC9V","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b9ff4eb0cd77f36","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"fibrocartilage"},"output":"Found 51 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nfibrochondrocyte progenitor cell \\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nFCP- related synonym - abbreviation - PMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. FCP demonstrates colony-forming capacity and multi-lineage differentiation potential toward osteogenic and adipogenic lineages. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\\n\\nPMID: [31871141](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31871141/)\\nPMID: [36338137](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36338137/)\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\n\\nMesenchymal cell\\nProgenitor cell \\n\\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\n\\nPart of some ‘ fibrocartilage’\\nexpresses some 'cell surface glycoprotein MUC18'\\nexpresses some 'myosin light chain kinase, smooth muscle'\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(I) chain'\\nexpresses some 'collagen alpha-1(III) chain'\\n\\n\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\nhttps://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\nI will add a link to fibrochondrocyte - 'develops from' some 'fibrochondrocyte progenitor cell' once the term is added\\n\",\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/reports/summary_release.md:\n  Line 1795: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000058 | chondroblast                                                                              |\n\n  Line 1796: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000134 | mesenchymal stem cell                                                                     |\n\n  Line 1797: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007001 | skeletogenic cell                                                                         |\n\n  Line 1798: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007009 | prechondroblast                                                                           |\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/imports/merged_import.owl:\n  Line 172538: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"ISBN:0073040584\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Intervertebral_disk\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001066> \"A pad of fibrocartilage between the articular surfaces of two successive vertebral centra which has nucleus pulposus at its core.\")\n\n  Line 172553: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"BTO:0003625\") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001066> \"intervertebral fibrocartilage\")\n\n  Line 180196: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001479> \"Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.[VSAO]\")\n\n  Line 190225: # Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> (fibrocartilage)\n\n  Line 190237: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165\") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"fibrocartilage tissue\")\n\n  Line 190242: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"The white fibrocartilages admit of arrangement into four groups-interarticular, connecting, circumferential, and stratiform -- WP. EDITOR NOTE: TODO add mineralized\")\n\n  Line 190243: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"fibrocartilage\")\n\n  Line 194896: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"FMA:FMA\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Symphysis\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002216> \"Cartilaginous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by fibrocartilage. Examples: pubic symphysis, intervertebral symphysis, manubriosternal joint.[FMA].\")\n\n  Line 194897: AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002216> \"consider adding fibrocartilage class\")\n\n  Line 199381: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002418> \"Previous: \\\"A portion of connective tissue dominated by extracellular matrix containing collagen type II and large amounts of proteoglycan, particularly chondroitin sulfate[GO]. Regular connective tissue, which consists of chondrocytes and related cells, the intercellular matrix of which is chondrified. Examples: hyaline cartilage, fibrocartilage, elastic cartilage[FMA]. an avascular supporting and articular skeletal tissue. It also functions as the primary endoskeletal support in vertebrate embryos. Cartilage is deposited by and is composed of chondroblasts and chondrocytes separated by an extracellular matrix, which may or may not mineralize depending on cartilage type, age, or taxon[Hall and Witten].\\\" See also FMA:71500 Set of cartilages, FMA:55107 Cartilage organ, FMA:12264 Articular cartilage. // elements made from cartilage, cartilage-like, or chondroid tissues evolved in invertebrates[H&W]\")\n\n  Line 220948: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"BTO:0003629\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Annulus_fibrosus_disci_intervertebralis\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004715> \"The ring of fibrocartilage and fibrous tissue forming the circumference of the intervertebral disc; surrounds the nucleus pulposus, which is prone to herniation when the annulus fibrosus is compromised.\")\n\n  Line 238460: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Cartilage_of_pharyngotympanic_tube\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007354> \"A triangular plate of elastic fibrocartilage that forms the cartilage component of the pharyngotympanic tube.\")\n\n  Line 249257: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"FMA:7491\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011134> \"Joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by ligaments or fibrocartilage without an intervening synovial cavity. Examples: sagittal suture, inferior tibiofibular syndesmosis, costochondral joint, pubic symphysis.\")\n\n  Line 253870: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0013631> \"Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.\")\n\n  Line 255745: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Lingual_septum\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0014790> \"The lingual septum consists of a vertical layer of fibrous tissue, extending throughout the entire length of the median plane of the tongue, though not quite reaching the dorsum. It is thicker behind than in front, and occasionally contains a small fibrocartilage, about 6 mm. in length. It is well displayed by making a vertical section across the organ.\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/diffs/cl-diff.md:\n  Line 6881: ### fibrocartilage `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995`\n\n  Line 6883: - [fibrocartilage](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995) SubClassOf [protein-containing material entity](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000050567) \n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 25601: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39759119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020018 \"A fibrochondrocyte located in fibrocartilage that exhibits active proliferation capacity and is in S phase of the cell cycle. It functions as a progenitor cell positioned at the root of developmental trajectories alongside fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP), with the capacity to diverge toward one of two developmental fates: (1) fibrochondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes, or (2) regulatory chondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes. It is characterised by co-expression of COL1A1, the growth factors FGF7 and CTGF, and the cell-cycle genes STMN1, KIAA0101, and MCM3 in humans. During early progenitor differentiation, FGF7 and COL1A1 expression increases and then declines as the cell commits to terminal fates.\")\n\n  Line 35326: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072104 \"A chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus. In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes. This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte.\")\n\n  Line 35328: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrocartilage chondrocyte\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/for_reference/Manchester_CL_normalisation_expt/owl/fma.owl:\n  Line 1672:             >Regular connective tissue, which consists of chondrocytes and related cells, the intercellular matrix of which is chondrified. Examples: hyaline cartilage, fibrocartilage, elastic cartilage.</def>\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/reports/summary_release.md:\n  Line 1795: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000058 | chondroblast                                                                              |\n\n  Line 1796: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0000134 | mesenchymal stem cell                                                                     |\n\n  Line 1797: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007001 | skeletogenic cell                                                                         |\n\n  Line 1798: | UBERON:0035847 | fibrocartilage enthesis                                          | has developmental contribution from            | CL:0007009 | prechondroblast                                                                           |\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/imports/merged_import.owl:\n  Line 172538: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"ISBN:0073040584\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Intervertebral_disk\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001066> \"A pad of fibrocartilage between the articular surfaces of two successive vertebral centra which has nucleus pulposus at its core.\")\n\n  Line 172553: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"BTO:0003625\") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001066> \"intervertebral fibrocartilage\")\n\n  Line 180196: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001479> \"Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.[VSAO]\")\n\n  Line 190225: # Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> (fibrocartilage)\n\n  Line 190237: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165\") <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"fibrocartilage tissue\")\n\n  Line 190242: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"The white fibrocartilages admit of arrangement into four groups-interarticular, connecting, circumferential, and stratiform -- WP. EDITOR NOTE: TODO add mineralized\")\n\n  Line 190243: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995> \"fibrocartilage\")\n\n  Line 194896: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"FMA:FMA\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Symphysis\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002216> \"Cartilaginous joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by fibrocartilage. Examples: pubic symphysis, intervertebral symphysis, manubriosternal joint.[FMA].\")\n\n  Line 194897: AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002216> \"consider adding fibrocartilage class\")\n\n  Line 199381: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002418> \"Previous: \\\"A portion of connective tissue dominated by extracellular matrix containing collagen type II and large amounts of proteoglycan, particularly chondroitin sulfate[GO]. Regular connective tissue, which consists of chondrocytes and related cells, the intercellular matrix of which is chondrified. Examples: hyaline cartilage, fibrocartilage, elastic cartilage[FMA]. an avascular supporting and articular skeletal tissue. It also functions as the primary endoskeletal support in vertebrate embryos. Cartilage is deposited by and is composed of chondroblasts and chondrocytes separated by an extracellular matrix, which may or may not mineralize depending on cartilage type, age, or taxon[Hall and Witten].\\\" See also FMA:71500 Set of cartilages, FMA:55107 Cartilage organ, FMA:12264 Articular cartilage. // elements made from cartilage, cartilage-like, or chondroid tissues evolved in invertebrates[H&W]\")\n\n  Line 220948: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"BTO:0003629\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Annulus_fibrosus_disci_intervertebralis\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004715> \"The ring of fibrocartilage and fibrous tissue forming the circumference of the intervertebral disc; surrounds the nucleus pulposus, which is prone to herniation when the annulus fibrosus is compromised.\")\n\n  Line 238460: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Cartilage_of_pharyngotympanic_tube\") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0007354> \"A triangular plate of elastic fibrocartilage that forms the cartilage component of the pharyngotympanic tube.\")\n\n  Line 249257: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"FMA:7491\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0011134> \"Joint in which the articulating bones or cartilages are connected by ligaments or fibrocartilage without an intervening synovial cavity. Examples: sagittal suture, inferior tibiofibular syndesmosis, costochondral joint, pubic symphysis.\")\n\n  Line 253870: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0013631> \"Sesamoids are often endochondral replacement elements and in addition to bone tissue, may also be composed of articular cartilage, fibrocartilage, hyaline cartilage, and calcified cartilage.\")\n\n  Line 255745: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> \"Wikipedia:Lingual_septum\") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0014790> \"The lingual septum consists of a vertical layer of fibrous tissue, extending throughout the entire length of the median plane of the tongue, though not quite reaching the dorsum. It is thicker behind than in front, and occasionally contains a small fibrocartilage, about 6 mm. in length. It is well displayed by making a vertical section across the organ.\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/diffs/cl-diff.md:\n  Line 6881: ### fibrocartilage `http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995`\n\n  Line 6883: - [fibrocartilage](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001995) SubClassOf [protein-containing material entity](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PR_000050567) \n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 25600: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39759119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020018 \"A fibrochondrocyte located in fibrocartilage that exhibits active proliferation capacity and is in S phase of the cell cycle. It functions as a progenitor cell positioned at the root of developmental trajectories alongside fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP), with the capacity to diverge toward one of two developmental fates: (1) fibrochondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes, or (2) regulatory chondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes. It is characterised by co-expression of COL1A1, the growth factors FGF7 and CTGF, and the cell-cycle genes STMN1, KIAA0101, and MCM3 in humans. During early progenitor differentiation, FGF7 and COL1A1 expression increases and then declines as the cell commits to terminal fates.\")\n\n  Line 35325: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28939894\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072104 \"A chondrocyte with hybrid fibroblastic-chondrogenic characteristics found in fibrocartilage, particularly in the avascular inner zone and transitional middle zone of the meniscus. In humans, fibrochondrocytes are marked by predominant expression of type I collagen (COL1A1) and fibril-associated collagens (COL3A1, COL6A1), while retaining type II collagen (COL2A1) expression and exhibiting lower SOX9 than hyaline chondrocytes. This molecular profile underlies the synthesis of abundant type I collagen essential for fibrocartilage matrix and reflects an intermediate phenotype between fibroblast and chondrocyte.\")\n\n  Line 35327: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34608249\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4072104 \"fibrocartilage chondrocyte\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/for_reference/Manchester_CL_normalisation_expt/owl/fma.owl:\n  Line 1672:             >Regular connective tissue, which consists of chondrocytes and related cells, the intercellular matrix of which is chondrified. Examples: hyaline cartilage, fibrocartilage, elastic cartilage.</def>\n","metadata":{"matches":51,"truncated":false},"title":"fibrocartilage","time":{"start":1778561838602,"end":1778561838641}},"id":"prt_e1a8bed4b001G266Gp9ck2VYhZ","sessionID":"ses_1e5750b97ffe2Ms6mBm22